__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){m.exports="# Workout Tracker Privacy Policy, Terms, and Health-Data Consent\n\n## Effective date\nNovember 1, 2026\n\n## 1. Controller\n\nThe controller is the developer and operator of Workout Tracker, based in Germany.\n\n**Contact:** [columcross@gmail.com](mailto:columcross@gmail.com)\n\nUse this address for privacy questions and requests for access, export, correction, restriction, consent withdrawal, or deletion.\n\n## 2. Data Processed\n\nWorkout Tracker may process:\n\n- your name, email address, Google sign-in information, Supabase user ID, and session information;\n- body weight and height;\n- exercise names, repetitions, lifted weights, workout times, timezone, and workout history;\n- the time at which you accepted this document;\n- an unfinished workout draft stored on your device; and\n- technical and security logs, including IP address, request times, authentication events, and errors.\n\n## 3. Purposes and Legal Bases\n\nData is processed to authenticate approved users, provide workout recording and history, restore unfinished drafts, secure and maintain the Service, respond to requests, and comply with legal obligations.\n\nThe legal bases are:\n\n- **Article 6(1)(a) and Article 9(2)(a) GDPR:** your explicit consent to processing body measurements and workout records that may reveal health information;\n- **Article 6(1)(b) GDPR:** providing and administering the Service you request;\n- **Article 6(1)(f) GDPR:** securing, troubleshooting, and preventing misuse of the Service; and\n- **Article 6(1)(c) GDPR:** compliance with applicable legal obligations.\n\nProviding health data is necessary for the Service's workout-tracking functions. If you do not consent, or later withdraw consent, those functions cannot be provided.\n\nWorkout Tracker does not sell personal data, use it for advertising, or make automated decisions producing legal or similarly significant effects.\n\n## 4. Explicit Health-Data Consent\n\nBody measurements and workout records may constitute health data under Article 9 GDPR. By selecting **Acknowledge and Accept**, you explicitly consent to their collection, storage, retrieval, and display for workout tracking, draft recovery, workout history, security, support, and data export.\n\nYou may withdraw consent at any time by deleting your account or emailing [columcross@gmail.com](mailto:columcross@gmail.com). Withdrawal does not affect processing that was lawful before withdrawal.\n\n## 5. Providers and International Transfers\n\nThe Service uses:\n\n- **Supabase** for authentication, database storage, APIs, backups, and operational logs;\n- **Google** for sign-in; and\n- the applicable web-hosting provider to deliver the application.\n\nThese providers receive only data needed to perform their services. Some providers or subprocessors may process data outside the European Economic Area. Where required, transfers rely on an adequacy decision, the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses, or another lawful safeguard. Information about applicable safeguards is available by contacting the Developer.\n\n## 6. Device Storage\n\nThe Service uses local browser or device storage for the authenticated session and unfinished workout draft. This storage is necessary to provide the requested functions and is not used for advertising or cross-site tracking. Drafts are removed after confirmed submission or when discarded on that device. You can also clear them through browser or device settings.\n\n## 7. Retention and Deletion\n\nAccount profiles, body measurements, and workouts are retained while your application account is active. Consent records, request correspondence, and security logs are retained only as long as needed to demonstrate compliance, resolve requests, secure the Service, or meet legal obligations.\n\nThe in-app **Delete account** action deletes your application profile and saved sets, exercises, and workouts, signs out the current device, and attempts to remove its draft. Authentication records, logs, offline-device copies, and temporary backup copies may require separate processing or remain until the relevant retention cycle expires. Email [columcross@gmail.com](mailto:columcross@gmail.com) to request complete erasure of other data held for the Service.\n\nData will be deleted when no longer necessary, when consent is withdrawn and no other lawful basis applies, or when otherwise required by Article 17 GDPR. Limited data may be retained where necessary for a legal obligation or legal claim.\n\n## 8. Terms of Use\n\nThe Service is a free, invitation-only workout-recording tool and is not a medical device or medical advice. You must use only your approved account and must not access another user's data, bypass security, interfere with the Service, or use it unlawfully.\n\nThe Service may be changed, interrupted, or discontinued. To the extent permitted by law, it is provided without a guarantee of uninterrupted availability. Nothing excludes liability that cannot be excluded under German or EU law. German law applies without limiting mandatory consumer or data-protection rights.\n\n## 9. Changes\n\nThis document may be updated when the Service, providers, processing, or law changes. If a change requires renewed consent, the Service will request it before continuing the affected processing.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nBy selecting **Acknowledge and Accept**, you confirm that you have read and accepted these terms and **explicitly consent to the health-data processing described in section 4**.\n"},1606,[]);
